/-!
# Analytic sets are universally measurable

This file proves Lusin's universal-measurability theorem: every analytic subset of a Hausdorff
space is measurable after completing any s-finite measure defined on a measurable space containing
the Borel sets. Equivalently, it differs from a measurable set by a null set. It also records the
generated-measurable-space consequence used by measurable selection.

Every finite Borel-compatible measure is a Choquet capacity (`TauCeti.IsChoquetCapacity.measure`),
so Choquet's capacitability theorem (`TauCeti.IsChoquetCapacity.exists_isCompact_subset_le_add`)
supplies inner compact approximations of arbitrary outer-measure accuracy on any Hausdorff space; an
s-finite measure has the same null sets as an equivalent finite measure, and a countable union of
inner compact approximations differs from the analytic set by a null set.

The theorem is classically stated for Polish ambient spaces, but the argument uses neither a metric
nor separability of the ambient space: the Baire-space closure step
(`TauCeti.iInter_closure_image_subset_image_Iic`) and Choquet's capacitability theorem hold in every
Hausdorff space, so the three universal-measurability statements below assume just `T2Space`.
`analyticSet_setOf_iInf_lt` assumes the standard Borel and second-countability hypotheses of
Mathlib's measurable-projection theorem `MeasurableSet.analyticSet_image`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.MeasureTheory.analyticSet_setOf_iInf_lt`: the strict sublevel of a pointwise infimum is
  analytic when the corresponding set before projection is measurable;
* `MeasureTheory.AnalyticSet.nullMeasurableSet`: an analytic subset of a Hausdorff space is
  null-measurable for every s-finite measure on a measurable space containing the Borel sets;
* `MeasureTheory.NullMeasurableSet.of_generateFrom_analyticSet`: the same holds for the measurable
  space generated by analytic sets;
* `TauCeti.MeasureTheory.nullMeasurable_of_measurable_generateFrom_analyticSet`: a function
  measurable for that generated measurable space is null-measurable for every such s-finite
  measure.

## Provenance

The proof is adapted from Daniel Lyng's Apache-2.0 Econlib development,
`Econlib/Math/MeasureTheory/AnalyticNullMeasurable.lean`, commit
`003655ccf010cdf44c4f67d6675167b54ce0e9df`, with the inner compact approximation factored out to
general Choquet capacities in `TauCeti.MeasureTheory.Constructions.Polish.Capacitability` and the
closure lemma generalized to Hausdorff spaces in `TauCeti.Topology.Instances.NatNat`.

## References

* A. S. Kechris, *Classical Descriptive Set Theory*, Springer-Verlag, 1995, Theorem 29.7, which
  states the result for Polish ambient spaces.
-/

public section

open Filter Set Topology

open scoped ENNReal

noncomputable section

namespace TauCeti

open _root_.MeasureTheory

namespace MeasureTheory

/-- Let `f` take values in a complete linear order. If its strict sublevel is measurable on the
product of two standard Borel spaces, the second carrying a second-countable topology whose open
sets are measurable, then the corresponding strict sublevel of the pointwise infimum over the first
factor is analytic. This is the measurable-projection principle used by infimal transforms. -/
theorem analyticSet_setOf_iInf_lt
    {X Y A : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X] [StandardBorelSpace X]
    [TopologicalSpace Y] [SecondCountableTopology Y] [MeasurableSpace Y] [StandardBorelSpace Y]
    [OpensMeasurableSpace Y] [CompleteLinearOrder A] (f : X × Y → A) (a : A)
    (h : MeasurableSet {z | f z < a}) :
    AnalyticSet {y | (⨅ x, f (x, y)) < a} := by
  convert h.analyticSet_image measurable_snd using 1
  ext y
  simp [iInf_lt_iff]

end MeasureTheory

end TauCeti

namespace MeasureTheory

variable {X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] [T2Space X] [MeasurableSpace X] [OpensMeasurableSpace X]

/-- **Lusin's universal-measurability theorem.** An analytic subset of a Hausdorff space is
null-measurable with respect to every s-finite measure on a measurable space containing the Borel
sets, equivalently measurable in the completion of that measure. -/
theorem AnalyticSet.nullMeasurableSet
    {S : Set X} (hS : AnalyticSet S) (μ : Measure X) [SFinite μ] :
    NullMeasurableSet S μ := by
  -- Pass to an equivalent finite measure and approximate `S` from inside by compact sets.
  obtain ⟨ν, _, hμν, -⟩ := exists_isFiniteMeasure_absolutelyContinuous (μ := μ)
  refine NullMeasurableSet.mono_ac ?_ hμν
  choose K hK hKS hνK using fun n : ℕ =>
    (TauCeti.IsChoquetCapacity.measure ν).exists_isCompact_subset_le_add hS
      (measure_ne_top ν S) (ε := (n : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹) (by simp)
  have hG : MeasurableSet (⋃ n, K n) := .iUnion fun n => (hK n).isClosed.measurableSet
  have hle : ν S ≤ ν (⋃ n, K n) :=
    ge_of_tendsto' (by simpa using tendsto_const_nhds.add ENNReal.tendsto_inv_nat_nhds_zero)
      fun n => (hνK n).trans (by gcongr; exact subset_iUnion K n)
  exact hG.nullMeasurableSet.congr (ae_eq_of_subset_of_measure_ge (iUnion_subset hKS) hle
    hG.nullMeasurableSet (measure_ne_top ν S))

/-- Every set in the measurable space generated by the analytic subsets of a Hausdorff space is
null-measurable for every s-finite measure on a measurable space containing the Borel sets. -/
theorem NullMeasurableSet.of_generateFrom_analyticSet
    {S : Set X} (μ : Measure X) [SFinite μ]
    (hS : MeasurableSet[MeasurableSpace.generateFrom {T : Set X | AnalyticSet T}] S) :
    NullMeasurableSet S μ :=
  nullMeasurable_generateFrom (f := id) (fun _ (hT : AnalyticSet _) => hT.nullMeasurableSet μ) hS

end MeasureTheory

namespace TauCeti.MeasureTheory

open _root_.MeasureTheory

/-- A function measurable for the measurable space generated by the analytic subsets of a
Hausdorff space is null-measurable for every s-finite measure on a measurable space containing the
Borel sets. -/
theorem nullMeasurable_of_measurable_generateFrom_analyticSet
    {X A : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] [T2Space X] [MeasurableSpace X] [OpensMeasurableSpace X]
    [MeasurableSpace A] {g : X → A} (μ : Measure X) [SFinite μ]
    (hg : Measurable[MeasurableSpace.generateFrom {T : Set X | AnalyticSet T}] g) :
    NullMeasurable g μ :=
  fun _ hs => NullMeasurableSet.of_generateFrom_analyticSet μ (hg hs)

end TauCeti.MeasureTheory
